  Scottish Parliament going down such a  route there has to be a way in that  scenario that the Scottish Parliament  the Scottish government can trigger a  referendum and of course in the previous  referendum we had the Edinburgh  agreement that was an agreement of the  two governments that that referendum  could take place Westminster can't just  hope this goes away it won't go away so  what is your next step then you say you  respect the Supreme Court decision my  message to the prime minister is is  recognize the reality of that mandate  that the Scottish Parliament the  Scottish government has we should have  talks that allows the Scottish  government to have a section 30  Authority that we can have that  referendum now I if we don't have that I  would regret that position but that then  means what the first Minister said that  the the next selection that we're going  to face as a Westminster one the only  option that we would have the only  realistic option option for now would be  to use that general election as a de  facto campaign for a Scottish reference  is there a problem though because what  you're doing there is you're saying that  people are voting in an election as if  it's a referendum but of course the  people vote in elections for all kinds  of different things we look at the  living standards issue that people are  now facing look at the NHS look at  schools look at Energy prices people can  vote for all kinds of different reasons  you can't just say they're definitely  just voting well on a binary issue we're  of course going to have a conference in  the early part of next year and we'll  debate all these things and we'll come  to a very firm conclusion about how  we're going to face this but we're in a  situation that Westminster is not  recognizing the harsh reality of a  government in Edinburgh that has that  mandate so if we have to look at  mechanisms such as using Innovation and  then we would have to appeal to the  people of Scotland to re