vestment as a  consequence of coming back in the  European Union it's about making sure  that we can deliver the economy that we  know that the people in Scotland look we  have seen a declining population on a  relative basis with the United Kingdom  for every decade for the last 150 years  we have to change the record I know  through green energy for example people  we can upscale our production five-fold  we can deliver 385 000 jobs in energy as  a consequence of doing this we have a  plan for delivering growth for  delivering prosperity of delivering on  our climate climate targets and we need  the powers of Independence to do that  why for example Westminster is holding  us back in carbon capture and storage  there are many examples I mean the  things that we would do that would  transform the Scottish economy now you  talk about trade and so on take Ireland  as an example you go back to the  post-war period more than 80 percent of  Ireland's trade was with the UK it's now  nine percent because they've grown the  overseas markets and actually over that  period And every year iron's trade with  the UK has grown there is a growth  opportunity that we will deliver on  delivering Prosperity driving down on  the poverty that we're inherenting from  the current regime it's a message of  Hope and we will do this we will win  this argument I think tonight there's a  lot of people in Scotland have a resolve  that we will not be silent and not be  stopped by the UK government not  recognizing democracy is it the truth of  it that you know in some ways it quite  suits the s p to be talking about  independence because it means you're not  talking about your record in Scotland  and what's currently happening in  Scotland I mean let's look at the NHS  for example the worst any waiting times  figures on records 6 000 vacancies in  nursing and Midwifery uh minutes of the  meeting of course of Scotland's NHS  leaders in September saying there's a  billion pound hole in the budget so it's  not possible to continue to run the  range of programs the NHS currently  offers while remaining safe and doing no  harm this is really frightening stuff  it's an absolute priority of the health  secretary and the government to improve  the outcomes in NHS Scotland we know the  responsibility that we've got to do that  right it's not good enough then yes I  admit that that has to be better look I  could say to you if you can trust the  performance of NHS Scotland against  other parts of the United Kingdom then  we outperform other parts of the United  Kingdom however we have to do better I  absolutely accept that but one of the  problems of all of this Sophie you look  at what happened last week with the  Autumn statement the fun something that  we get is largely driven by the  consequence of the UK budget and our  budget in real terms has been cut this  year that's the reality we don't have  the borrowing parts we know that we need  to drive investment into our Public  Services look at what's going to happen  in the UK over the next four years five  years 30 billion pounds of cuts to the  public space it's not just about money  though is it look at these minutes  minutes again everything is a top  priority what is the real Focus it's a  managing issue as well isn't it you know  I can talk about my own health board at  nhsi and then I've got some great people  there that are leading that organization  but we've come through the covert crisis  there's a backlog that we have to  contend with and we should applaud those  are working really hard in our NHS the  other thing of course is that they are  discussing the possibility of a two-tier  Health System let's just rule that out  completely that will not happen where  the wealthy will pay for treatment that  will certainly not happen in Scotland  whether that's in the current status or  in an independent Scotland NHS care will  be free at the point of use for everyone  I'm interested to know your thoughts on